Subject: [PATCH] agent: its document dumps and traces to em's debug channel, the keys out

em_agent passed its journal's cap (1000 lines per 30 s) all the time, not only at its
start: in one lab bring-up (rdk-1004, 6 October 2026) the gateway's agent wrote 8,744 lines,
3,274 in its busiest 30 s, and a Wi-Fi extender's 20,913, 4,463 in its busiest 30 s. Most of
it was whole JSON documents printed one field to a line: each Link Report OneWifi publishes
(which the agent then drops), each Unassociated STA Link Metrics query subdoc and response,
OneWifi's device configuration at the agent's start and every subdoc the agent sends OneWifi
(those two the whole of an onboarding burst: 2,288 of the gateway agent's 2,739 lines in its
busiest 30 s); the rest per-message traces (the M2 attributes, each BSS's VAP, each operating
class, each metrics query routed). The first ones and the traces now print through
em_util_dbg_print, as 0237 does (/nvram/emAgentDbg, /nvram/emConfDbg); the device
configuration and the subdocs print their name and size only. Those two documents carry
every network's passphrase, and the agent also printed every network's key on the journal
twice per M2 (the parsed network key attribute and the new configuration's passphrase): the
keys are out of every line, journal and debug channel alike, and out of the BSS
configuration dump; the attribute line gives the key's length. The AP Metrics Response line
stays on the journal.

Upstream-Status: Pending

